Error [jet.TypestateUnknownState]: `Stuffed` is not a declared state of `Crate`
  --> tests/ui/typestate/unknown_state_in_marker_is_e0151.jet:9:5
    |
  9 |     #State(Stuffed) get: fn(self) -[]> Int {
    |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: Typestate: `Crate: struct { state { … } }` defines the valid state labels; `Stuffed` is not among them — a typo here would silently create a phantom state that no transition reaches
 Fix: Add `Stuffed` inside `Crate: struct { state { … } }`, or correct the spelling
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0151

Error [jet.TypestateWrongState]: `get` needs `Crate` in state `Stuffed`, but `b` is in state `Full`
  --> tests/ui/typestate/unknown_state_in_marker_is_e0151.jet:16:13
    |
 16 |     print(b.get())
    |             ^^^
 Why: Typestate: `get` is only valid in state `Stuffed`; calling it in `Full` is the out-of-order-events bug it prevents
 Fix: Transition `b` into state `Stuffed` before calling `get`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0150
